   "gap": "thm:p15-nda-examples (body lines 206-235, annex annex:p15.nda-examples lines 686-743) is not complete in the success condition's terms. Part 3 states the conclusion for every symmetric law with P(|X|>x)=x^{-alpha} (x>=1, 0<alpha<2), but the annex proof computes H_X only for 'one concrete law' with density (alpha/2)|x|^{-1-alpha} on |x|>1: it does not show that the hypothesis fixes the law of |X| (in particular P(|X|<=1)=0), so that H_X(x)=(alpha/(2-alpha))(x^{2-alpha}-1) and q_X(x)=x^{-alpha} hold for every law covered by the statement; it does not derive the stated limit (2-alpha)/alpha of x^2 q_X(x)/H_X(x); and it does not verify the nondegeneracy hypothesis that the characterization it invokes requires. Part 1's claim that the scale sqrt(n E X^2) 'yields limiting variance sigma^2/E X^2' leaves the centering unstated (the proof silently uses n mu). Owed in the editable annex host handbook/annex/p15/normal-domains-of-attraction.tex: write these proof steps and name the centering n mu in the part-1 argument. The statement wording of part 1 lies in the readonly body handbook/parts/p15/normal-domains-of-attraction.tex lines 208-212 (lead-owned edit).",
   "blocker": {
    "kind": "lead_owned",
    "ref": "readonly body handbook/parts/p15/normal-domains-of-attraction.tex lines 208-212 (thm:p15-nda-examples part 1): the statement gives a limiting variance for the scale sqrt(n E X^2) without naming the centering (S_n - n mu); the statement must name it (unstated-assumption failure condition of ED26-P15-CH-normal-domains-of-attraction-C010)."
   }
